/T (The security analysis of the target website reveals that several important HTTP security headers are missing. As shown in the screenshot, the website received a grade of F, indicating poor security configuration. Critical headers such as Content-Security-Policy, X-Frame-Options, X-Content-Type-Options, Referrer-Policy, and Permissions-Policy are not implemented. These headers play a key role in protecting the website from common web-based attacks by controlling how browsers handle content and enforce security rules. The absence of these headers increases the exposure of the application to client-side attacks and reduces overall security posture.)
